# Ignore everything in Foundry Data by default
/*

# Keep repo meta files
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# -----------------------------
# Track custom module
# -----------------------------

!/modules/
/modules/*
!/modules/fabula-ultima-companion/
!/modules/fabula-ultima-companion/**

# Ignore old nested Git backup if it exists
/modules/fabula-ultima-companion/.git_BACKUP/

# -----------------------------
# Track game system
# -----------------------------

!/systems/
/systems/*
!/systems/custom-system-builder/
!/systems/custom-system-builder/**

# -----------------------------
# Track world
# -----------------------------

!/worlds/
/worlds/*
!/worlds/fabula-ultima-2/
!/worlds/fabula-ultima-2/**

# Save blobs are PERSONAL — never track, never push. The negation above
# un-ignores everything under the world, so before this rule a save slot was
# protected only by a per-file `skip-worktree` on the slots that happened to be
# tracked already. A NEW slot had no protection at all: `git add -A worlds/`
# staged slot-3.json on 2026-08-20. This makes the protection structural.
# (index.json / slot-1 / slot-2 remain tracked-but-skip-worktree from before;
# an ignore cannot untrack them, and untracking is a separate decision.)
/worlds/*/fu-saves/

# NOTE: Co-dev transfer scope (ship only actors+items+folders) is enforced
# LOCALLY on this clone, NOT here — a committed ignore would also block the
# co-dev from pushing those collections back to us. The local-only exclusion
# lives in .git/info/exclude (new shards) + `git update-index --skip-worktree`
# (existing tracked shards). See the codev-transfer-scope memory.

# -----------------------------
# Track repo docs and scripts
# -----------------------------

!/README.md
!/ONBOARDING.md
!/required-modules.json
!/setup.ps1

# -----------------------------
# Track local tooling
# -----------------------------

!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/check-esm.js
!/tools/camp-landing-phase-check.js
!/tools/safe-edit/
!/tools/safe-edit/**
!/tools/parse-fu-pdfs/
!/tools/parse-fu-pdfs/**
!/tools/csb-template/
!/tools/csb-template/**
!/tools/anim-studio/
!/tools/anim-studio/**
!/tools/skill-regression/
!/tools/skill-regression/**
# runtime marker written by the regression Stop-hook gate — local only
/tools/skill-regression/.state/
# The 2026-07 skill-regression expansion is now SHARED with the co-dev
# (bench / verify / expectations / hooks / ephemeral fixtures). Two caveats they
# need on first use — both documented in tools/skill-regression/README.md:
#   1. goldens/*.json fingerprint the AUTHORING world's content. On a divergent
#      world every skill reads as "changed", so run `capture` ONCE to establish
#      a local baseline before trusting `check`.
#   2. hooks/ arrives inert: the PostToolUse/Stop wiring lives in
#      .claude/settings.json, which is NOT tracked. Opt in deliberately.
# carrier-scan answers "is this content actually implemented?" against the
# authored export. Shared: it reads the same _authored-export the co-dev already
# reviews, needs no local state, and its whole point is that the nine-carrier
# rule stops living in one person's head.
!/tools/carrier-scan/
!/tools/carrier-scan/**
!/tools/hot-reload-map/
!/tools/hot-reload-map/**
!/tools/bug-report/
!/tools/bug-report/**
# mindscape — offline Monte Carlo combat model. Shared: it is a balance tool
# with no local state, and its ruleset spec (docs/mindscape-ruleset.md) is
# meant to be reviewed and disagreed with by whoever is tuning a fight.
!/tools/mindscape/
!/tools/mindscape/**
# node_modules is resolved from tools/safe-edit — mindscape must never carry one
/tools/mindscape/node_modules/

# -----------------------------
# Shared bug reports (see reports/README.md)
# -----------------------------
# One markdown file per report, announced on pull by the post-merge /
# post-checkout hooks. Deliberately tracked: a report is the handoff between the
# two of us, so it has to travel with the code it describes.
!/reports/
!/reports/**

# -----------------------------
# LevelDB runtime files — never commit these.
# .ldb, MANIFEST-*, CURRENT are the actual data and SHOULD be committed.
# LOCK, LOG are process-level state that must NOT be committed.
# Rule: always close Foundry cleanly before git add/commit.
# -----------------------------

**/LOCK
**/LOG
**/LOG.old

# Numbered write-ahead logs (e.g. 000001.log) — empty after clean shutdown.
# Excluding them avoids stale WAL conflicts when a peer opens the DB.
/worlds/fabula-ultima-2/data/**/*.log
/worlds/fabula-ultima-2/packs/**/*.log
/systems/custom-system-builder/packs/**/*.log

# -----------------------------
# Test bridge — file-based IPC between Claude and the running world.
# Inbox/outbox/state/secret are session-local and should never be committed.
# -----------------------------

/worlds/fabula-ultima-2/test-bridge/

# -----------------------------
# world-export local checkpoint — `.baseline/` is a private "last reviewed"
# snapshot for the `--since-baseline` workflow. Never shared; never committed.
# The rest of _authored-export/ IS committed (it's the reviewable artifact).
# -----------------------------

/worlds/*/_authored-export/.baseline/

# world-pack merge-rebuild scratch (CLI unpack/pack working dirs) — never committed.
/worlds/*/_merge-work/

# -----------------------------
# Ignore archive / temp files
# -----------------------------

*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.tmp
*.temp
*.lock

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Auto-playtest journals (sim debug output, not world data)
worlds/*/sim-logs/

# Fabula Ultima source PDFs — the canonical rules reference for skill authoring,
# at /reference/fabula-pdfs/. Already covered by the blanket `/*` at the top of
# this file (nothing at root is tracked unless explicitly un-ignored); recorded
# here only so the omission reads as deliberate. They are the publisher's
# copyrighted books, so this directory must never gain an `!` exception.
